  "prequalification_correction": "Earlier passing private batches included an implicit widening step for narrow+script. Microsoft mapping guidance requires explicit FULLWIDTH for halfwidth-to-Hiragana conversion. Removed the extra widening and replaced those candidate expectations with narrow/script preservation controls; only qualified batches count as current evidence.",
  "references": [
    "https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/access/functions/strconv-function",
    "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/intl/handling-sorting-in-your-applications",
    "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winnls/nf-winnls-lcmapstringex"
  ],
  "contracts": [
    "Thirty-two compatible Japanese shape/case flags are admitted, adding 27 verified baseline refusals. Exact LCID 1041 is mandatory; no aliases or host locale inferred.",
    "The explicit engineering order is case first, requested wide, requested script, then requested narrow. No implicit fullwidth transformation or fictitious halfwidth Hiragana.",
    "Existing public case/encoding Conversion recipes remain unchanged. Unknown/contradictory flags and shape+encoding refuse before source admission.",
    "Each operation uses existing ICU/width/kana services and their qualified mappings. No new normalization table, dependency, stored carrier or default allowance.",
    "Raw range publication, source/control eager errors, NULL handling, prepared parameter reuse, per-Text ceilings and cumulative bytes/work/cancellation remain explicit.",
    "Derived/correlated/grouped query composition and CLI buffered errors pass. Native ordering/NLS/Access qualification and independent combined-mode Unicode replay remain separate next evidence work."
  ],
